All periodic damage/heal ticks scale their interval with caster haste.

Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Auras/SpellAuraEffects.cpp,
AuraEffect::CalculatePeriodic

Why: player request 2026-08-26 -- "make any kind of damage-over-time or
heal-over-time effects scale with haste... don't reduce duration, just
increase how quickly damage/healing ticks occur."

Upstream, the caster's UNIT_MOD_CAST_SPEED (spell haste; <1 = faster) only
shrinks a periodic's tick amplitude when the spell carries
SPELL_ATTR5_SPELL_HASTE_AFFECTS_PERIODIC or is hit by a
SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_HASTE affect-mask aura. Everything else -- the vast
majority of DoTs and HoTs -- ticks at a fixed interval forever.

The change drops that gate: every periodic AuraEffect now scales its
amplitude by the caster's current haste. Because GetTotalTicks() is
MaxDuration/amplitude, shrinking the amplitude raises the tick count within
the SAME duration. A 10-second DoT that ticked once per second now ticks
every 0.8s at 20% haste and delivers 12 ticks instead of 10 -- the duration
is untouched, only the cadence (and therefore total output) changes. This
is the classic "haste makes DoTs/HoTs stronger without shortening them"
feel, applied server-wide.

Deliberate scope notes:
- Applies to creatures as well as players (caster may be any Unit); a
  hasted enemy's DoTs tick faster too, which is symmetric and fine.
- Channeled spells reach this code through SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_TRIGGER_SPELL;
  their totalTicks scales identically, so a hasted channel delivers more
  ticks over the same channel -- consistent with the request.
- No duration is touched anywhere; only m_amplitude changes, and the tick
  loop's `(m_tickNumber+1) > totalTicks` guard uses the scaled count, so
  there is no over-tick and no early expiry.

Verified against SpellAuraEffects.cpp:934-955 (tick loop) and :7072
(GetTotalTicks) at the time of writing.
